{% assign lts_schedule = include.lts_schedule | default: site.data.learn_to_scull_schedule %}
{% assign cohort = include.cohort %}
{% assign program_number = cohort.name | default: page.lts_program_number | default: "[LTS#]" %}
{% assign session_dates = cohort.session_dates | default: page.session_dates %}
{% assign next_session = session_dates[1] | default: "[Day, Date, Time]" %}
{% assign instructors = cohort.coaches | default: page.instructors %}
{% assign public_site_url = site.url | append: site.baseurl %}
Dear {{ program_number }} Participants,<br><br>

Great job at our first Learn to Scull session!<br><br>

**Key Achievements From Session 1**<br>
*   Reiterated the basic rowing motion using ergometers.<br>
*   Got familiar with equipment terminology and boat handling.<br>
*   Attempted the essential "flip test" to practice water safety.<br>
*   Built comfort and confidence around rowing equipment and water.<br><br>

**Preparing for Session 2: Hitting the Water**<br>
To build on what you've learned, you can prepare for our first on-water session by reviewing the following:<br>
1.  **Video Resources for Session 2:** Watch the [Session 2 Videos]({{ public_site_url }}/for-learners/technique/videos.html?filter=session2) to see these concepts in action.<br>
2.  Review the [Session 2 Learning Guide]({{ public_site_url }}/for-learners/learning-journey/session-2.html) for an overview of what we'll cover.<br><br>

**Next Session: {{ next_session }}**<br>
We'll focus on:<br>
*   Equipment Preparation and Transport<br>
*   Transferring ergometer stroke sequence to on-water rowing.<br>
*   Establishing proper recovery sequence (arms → body → slide).<br>
*   Developing basic boat control and balance.<br>
*   Mastering safe launching and landing procedures.<br><br>

**Reminders**<br>
*   Please arrive 10 minutes early.<br>
*   Wear suitable clothing (forecast: {{ page.weather_forecast | default: "[weather summary]" }}).<br>
*   Bring water and sun protection<br>
*   Towel and full change of clothes (just in case)<br><br>

If you have any questions before our next session, please don't hesitate to contact us.<br><br>

Best regards,<br><br>
{% include communication_templates/signature.liquid instructors=instructors lts_schedule=lts_schedule %}
